<p>Now, let=E2=80=99s consider what traversal algorithm we should use to po=
pulate this hash map.</p>
<p><strong>Breadth-first search</strong><br>
<!-- -->In general, we can employ any traversal method to assign column ids=
 to each node, as long as we increment the column id whenever we move right=
 and decrement it whenever we move left. However, we need to be cautious ab=
out the following two requirements:</p>
<ol>
<li>
<p>Nodes in the same column should be ordered from top to bottom.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Nodes in the same row and column should be ordered from left to right.</=
p>
</li>
</ol>
<p>So, we=E2=80=99ll need an algorithm that traverses the tree from top to =
bottom and then from left to right. This calls for <strong>BFS</strong>.</p=
>
<p>BFS processes nodes level by level, starting from the root and moving ho=
rizontally across the tree at each level. This method ensures nodes are vis=
ited from top to bottom, and for nodes in the same row (level), they are vi=
sited from left to right.</p>
